---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy and Public Access | Bureau of Digital Antiquities"
  description="Privacy information for the Bureau of Digital Antiquities public website, including data processing, cookies, analytics and contact information."
>
  <section class="page-header">
    <p class="section-label">Institutional Information</p>

    <h1>Privacy and Public Access</h1>

    <p class="page-introduction">
      This notice explains how information is handled when accessing the
      Bureau of Digital Antiquities public website.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="record-section">
    <div class="record-section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Public Website</p>
      <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="record-prose">
      <p>
        The Bureau website is primarily a static public information service.
        It does not provide public user accounts, comments, submissions or
        other facilities that require visitors to provide personal
        information through the website.
      </p>

      <p>
        The Bureau does not intentionally collect personal information from
        visitors unless there is a defined operational purpose for doing so.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="record-section">
    <div class="record-section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Technical Processing</p>
      <h2>Website Delivery and Security</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="record-prose">
      <p>
        The website uses Cloudflare infrastructure for hosting, content
        delivery, DNS and security. Technical information associated with
        requests to the website may therefore be processed by Cloudflare for
        purposes including delivery of website content, detection of malicious
        traffic and protection of the public service.
      </p>

      <p>
        Such technical information may include network and request information
        such as IP addresses, request paths, browser or user-agent information,
        timestamps and security-related request characteristics.
      </p>

      <p>
        Security and operational records are retained according to the
        facilities and retention periods provided by the Cloudflare services
        in use. The Bureau does not maintain a separate long-term visitor
        tracking database for the public website.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="record-section">
    <div class="record-section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Cookies and Analytics</p>
      <h2>Tracking Technologies</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="record-prose">
      <p>
        The Bureau does not use advertising trackers or third-party visitor
        analytics on the public website.
      </p>

      <p>
        The Bureau does not intentionally set application cookies for ordinary
        use of the public website. Security or infrastructure services may use
        technical mechanisms when required to protect or operate the service.
      </p>

      <p>
        If functionality requiring additional cookies, analytics or personal
        information is introduced in the future, this notice will be reviewed
        and updated accordingly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="record-section">
    <div class="record-section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Correspondence</p>
      <h2>Contacting the Bureau</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="record-prose">
      <p>
        Correspondence sent to the Bureau by email necessarily contains
        information supplied by the sender. Such information is used for the
        purpose of receiving and responding to the correspondence.
      </p>

        <p>
        General enquiries may be sent to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:contact@digitalantiquities.org">
            contact@digitalantiquities.org
        </a>.
        </p>

        <p>
        Security issues and vulnerability reports should be sent to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:security@digitalantiquities.org">
            security@digitalantiquities.org
        </a>.
        </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="record-section">
  <div class="record-section-heading">
    <p class="section-label">Institutional Status</p>
    <h2>About This Project</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="record-prose">
    <p>
      The Bureau of Digital Antiquities is a fictional institution. This
      website is an independent creative and educational project concerned
      with the documentation and presentation of digital history and digital
      preservation.
    </p>

    <p>
      Bureau offices, programmes, institutional records and administrative
      activities presented by this website form part of that fictional
      framework unless otherwise indicated. Historical websites, software,
      organisations, technologies and events documented by the Bureau may,
      however, refer to real-world subjects.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="record-section">
  <div class="record-section-heading">
    <p class="section-label">Copyright and Attribution</p>
    <h2>Third-Party and Historical Material</h2>
  </div>

  <div class="record-prose">
    <p>
      Names, trademarks, screenshots, archival captures and other third-party
      material referenced or reproduced by the Bureau remain subject to the
      rights of their respective owners.
    </p>

    <p>
      Where third-party or archival material is reproduced, the Bureau seeks
      to identify its source and provenance with the relevant record where
      practicable. The inclusion of such material does not imply endorsement
      by, affiliation with or ownership by the Bureau.
    </p>

    <p>
      Original Bureau text, graphics and other project material should be
      distinguished from third-party material documented as part of the
      historical record. Permission to use original Bureau material should not
      be assumed to extend to third-party works.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

  <section class="record-section">
    <div class="record-section-heading">
      <p class="section-label">Notice Administration</p>
      <h2>Changes to This Notice</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="record-prose">
      <p>
        This notice may be revised when the Bureau introduces new public
        services or makes material changes to the way the website processes
        information.
      </p>

      <p>
        Last reviewed: September 2026.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>